{"ts":"2026-09-19T11:22:29Z","event":"issue","plan":"0001-release-please-binary-artifacts","phase":4,"task":"TASK-015","message":"RISK-004 is false as stated: GNU tar unlinks an existing file before extracting, so untarring over a running binary succeeds (exit 0, running process keeps the deleted inode). The kernel rule is real but only for O_TRUNC, which tar does not do. TASK-015's justification therefore does not hold; asking the user before keeping a sudo rm -rf in the install path","detail":{"experiment":{"open O_WRONLY|O_TRUNC on running exe":"OSError 26 Text file busy","tar -C dest -xzf over running exe":"exit 0, /proc/PID/exe becomes (deleted)","platform":"Linux 7.0.0-30-generic, GNU tar"}}}
